## Shared project workflow

Start with `agentboard brief`, then read `.platform/work/BRIEF.md` and `.platform/work/ACTIVE.md`.
For an existing task run `agentboard handoff <slug>` and follow its load order and Resume state.
Use the user's stated task to select work; ask which stream only when the intent is ambiguous.

Before non-trivial new work, create or update the focused domain inventory, register a stream
with `agentboard new-stream`, and point BRIEF.md at it. Trivial fixes need no ceremony.
Load only relevant domain/reference files; do not load archives or the full memory pack by default.

For complex work, use `.platform/workflow.md` and the relevant `ab-*` skill.
Use available provider roles for bounded parallel work; never require an unavailable model.
An unapproved Execution brief prohibits implementation; ask the owner to approve it.
Preserve unrelated changes and user content. Run relevant tests; show evidence before claiming success.
Never commit, publish, perform destructive actions, or close a stream without the owner's authorization.

Before ending work or changing providers, save a checkpoint:
`agentboard checkpoint <slug> --what "what changed" --next "next action"`.
Log only known token counters and the actual provider/model. For cumulative counters pass
a stable `--session-id` (or `AGENTBOARD_SESSION_ID`) unique to the provider session.

For closure, run `agentboard close <slug>` for the harvest checklist, then show the owner the evidence.
Only the owner approves closure, by running `agentboard close <slug> --approve` themselves.
"Close it" from the user is not that approval. Never edit approval metadata, tick a criterion the owner owns, or move a stream file by hand.
`agentboard close <slug> --confirm` is the only archival path; run it only after the owner's approval.
Hooks are guardrails, not proof of identity; the CLI checks the recorded approval and completed criteria.

Keep provider-specific instructions outside this managed block; sync preserves them.
